cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these scripts, please cite them as below."
title: "PISA Analysis Scripts (2000-2022)"
authors:
  - family-names: "Speed"
    given-names: "Joe"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/Joe-Speed/pisa-scripts"
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-03-10
abstract: >-
  Python scripts for cleaning and analysing OECD PISA student questionnaire
  microdata (2000-2022), produced for an MSc dissertation at the University
  of Glasgow on adolescent reading behaviour. Covers books at home, daily
  reading time and reading attitudes across waves, and regressions of
  metacognitive outcomes on reading behaviour in PISA 2018.
